### 57.5 Completion on the strict branch

Every point in the closed cube (57.22) belongs to a terminal leaf.
A signed row leaf cannot contain a common zero. An \(E\) leaf can
contain one only at \(e=0,s=-1/5,t=-2/5\), by Lemma 57.2. Direct
substitution into the definitions (55.24)–(55.27) makes all four rows
zero at this stratum, for every proper-chart coordinate. This proves
the stronger closed polynomial assertion (57.3), while retaining its
pole explicitly.

The strict seed domain (57.2) has \(e>0\), so contains no such point.
Both proper charts, their overlap endpoints, and reciprocal infinity
were included in the proof. The negative half follows from (56.3),
and the central closed half from Proposition 56.1. No exceptional
linear-row branch was removed: all four necessary rows were kept
throughout. The actual channel exchange used at the start is valid on
the sign-symmetric complete open interval.

Finally,
\[
a^2=\frac{b^2(3-b^2)}{1+b^2},\qquad
\frac{d(a^2)}{d(b^2)}=
\frac{(1-b^2)(3+b^2)}{(1+b^2)^2}>0\quad(|b|<1).
\tag{57.32}
\]
Thus the remaining band is exactly
\(\sqrt{11/20}<|a|<1\), adjoining the inclusive interval already
excluded in Proposition 56.1. The original column-basis statement
follows from the unitary basis-direction argument at the end of §55.
This completes the proof of Proposition 57.1.

